# THE TITHE — MARS.
#
# The brief: a secret billionaires' lifeboat under the dust. Domes, servo
# units, mining rovers and companion fembots that smile, listen and upload
# every word. The reveal is the rent: THE FOUNDER only LEASES this planet, the
# landlords are older, scaled and cold-blooded, and their tithe has lately
# started asking for warm things.
#
# THREE DECISIONS.
#
#   IT IS A BROCHURE. Bright, confident, synthetic B♭ major. A jingle with a
#   hook, glass sparkling two octaves up, a presentation clicker on the
#   off-beats. It is sincere: this is how the colony sells itself, and nothing
#   in the arrangement is winking. (Where the moon was awe and HQ was a lobby,
#   Mars is a PITCH — the western squint this track used to wear went to Boot
#   Hill, which is where a western belongs.)
#
#   THE TITHE. A drum below the kick, every SIX sixteenths against a bar of
#   sixteen, so it walks across the brochure's 4/4 and lands with it once every
#   three bars and never otherwise. It is older than the calendar the brochure
#   is printed on and it does not care what beat anybody else is counting.
#
#   THE LANDLORDS COME DOWN A SEMITONE AT A TIME. Every section ends on a bare
#   chromatic fall in the tune — four notes, sliding, under a chord that was
#   supposed to cadence — and the break section is nothing BUT that: eight
#   bars, one semitone a bar, G down to C, with the advert switched off.
#
# Compile:  node scripts/song-import.mjs content/songs/red_dust.song --sheet

id     red_dust
title  THE TITHE
about
  Mars sells itself: a bright B♭-major brochure with a hook, glass sparkling
  two octaves above the pitch, a clicker on the off-beats and not one wink in
  the whole arrangement. Underneath it a drum lands every six sixteenths
  against a bar of sixteen — the landlords' tithe, walking across the
  presentation's 4/4 and agreeing with it once every three bars — and every
  section ends on a bare chromatic fall where the cadence should be. The break
  is that fall on its own: eight bars, one semitone each, the advert switched
  off and something cold-blooded counting down. Original melodies; nothing
  sampled.
tempo  136

# ── THE CAST ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The brochure's own voice. Bright, forward, and it means every word.
voice jingle square vol=.03 gate=.8 detune=6 echo=.25 vib=5.5/12/180
# The domes: a glassy sine two octaves over the pitch, drenched in echo.
voice shine  sine vol=.012 gate=.3 pan=.35 echo=.45
# The clicker — chord tones on the off-beat, mid, thin, slightly out of tune.
voice stab   square vol=.014 gate=.22 detune=12 pan=-0.3
voice bass   triangle vol=.055 gate=.75
# THE LANDLORDS. A lowpassed saw, and it only ever goes down.
voice cold   sawtooth vol=.018 gate=.9 lp=1400 pan=-0.15 echo=.3

# ── THE KIT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
drum kick    triangle vol=.058 gate=1 slide=.25 note=D2
drum snare   noise vol=.032 gate=.7 hp=1500
drum hat     noise vol=.0105 gate=.22 hp=7000 pan=.28
# THE TITHE — an octave under the kick, every sixth sixteenth. Bars 1 and 4 of
# the grid agree with the downbeat; bars 2 and 3 do not, and that is the point.
drum tithe   triangle vol=.07 gate=1 slide=.4 note=A1

# ── INTRO — the tithe is already running when the presentation starts ───────
section intro
  chords Bb | Bb | F | F
  tithe  x.....x.....x...|..x.....x.....x.|....x.....x.....|x.....x.....x...
  bass   .*16 | .*16 | four:2 | four:2
  stab   .*16 | .*16 | .*16 | offbeat:4
  shine  .*16 | .*16 | arp16:6 | arp16:6
  hat    ................|................|..x...x...x...x.|..x...x...x...x.

# ── A — the pitch. Bar 8 is where the cadence should be ────────────────────
section a
  chords Bb | Dm | Gm | Eb | Bb | F | Eb | F
  jingle a#4*4 d5*4 f5*8 | a5*4 f5*4 d5*8 | g5*4 a#5*4 d6*8 | c6*4 a#5*4 g5*8
         f5*4 a#5*4 d6*8 | c6*8 a5*8 | a#5*4 g5*4 d#5*8 | c5*4 b4*4 a#4*4 a4*4
  shine  arp16 6
  stab   offbeat 4
  bass   pump 2
  kick   x.....x.x.......|x.......x.x.....
  snare  ....x.......x...
  hat    x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x.
  tithe  x.....x.....x...|..x.....x.....x.|....x.....x.....|x.....x.....x...

# ── B — THE OFFER. Higher, warmer, and it still ends sliding ───────────────
section b
  chords Eb | F | Gm | Gm | Eb | F | Bb | Bb
  jingle d#5*4 g5*4 a#5*8 | c6*4 a5*4 f5*8 | g5*4 a#5*4 d6*4 f6*4 | d6*8 a#5*8
         g5*4 a#5*4 d#6*8 | d6*4 c6*4 a5*8 | a#5*8 f5*8 | d5*4 c#5*4 c5*4 b4*4
  shine  arp16 6
  stab   offbeat 4
  bass   gallop 2
  kick   x.....x.x.......|x.......x.x.....
  snare  ....x.......x...
  hat    x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x.
  tithe  x.....x.....x...|..x.....x.....x.|....x.....x.....|x.....x.....x...

# ── BREAK — the advert stops. One semitone a bar, and the tithe keeps time ──
section tithe_break
  chords Gm | Gm | Ebm | Ebm | Cm | Cm | Db | Db
  cold   g4*12 .*4 | f#4*12 .*4 | f4*12 .*4 | e4*12 .*4
         d#4*12 .*4 | d4*12 .*4 | c#4*12 .*4 | c4*12 .*4
  bass   g2*8 .*8 | .*16 | d#2*8 .*8 | .*16
         c2*8 .*8 | .*16 | c#2*8 .*8 | c#2*8 g#2*8
  tithe  x.....x.....x...|..x.....x.....x.|....x.....x.....|x.....x.....x...

# ── BUILD — the closing slide, taken upward for once ───────────────────────
section build
  chords Gm | A | Bb | C | Dm | Eb | F | F
  jingle g5*16 | a5*16 | a#5*16 | c6*16
         d6*8 f6*8 | d#6*8 a#5*8 | c6*4 a5*4 f5*8 | c6*4 f6*4 a6*8
  stab   offbeat 4
  shine  arp16 6
  bass   pump 2
  kick   x.......x.......
  snare  ....x.......x...|....x.......x...|....x.......x.x.|....x.......x.x.
         ....x...x.x.x.x.|....x...x.x.x.x.|x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x.|xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
  hat    x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x.
  tithe  x.....x.....x...|..x.....x.....x.|....x.....x.....|x.....x.....x...

# ── TURN — the pitch at full volume, and the same slide at the end of it ───
section turn
  chords Bb | Dm | Gm | Eb | Bb | F | Eb | F
  jingle f5*2 g5*2 a5*2 a#5*2 d6*8 | f6*4 d6*4 a5*8 | a#5*4 d6*4 g6*4 f6*4 | d#6*8 a#5*8
         d6*4 f6*4 d6*4 a#5*4 | c6*8 f5*8 | g5*4 a#5*4 d#6*8 | c6*4 b5*4 a#5*4 a5*4
  cold   .*16 | .*16 | .*16 | .*16
         .*16 | .*16 | .*16 | c5*4 b4*4 a#4*4 a4*4
  shine  arp16 6
  stab   stab 4
  bass   gallop 2
  kick   x.....x.x.......|x.......x.x.....
  snare  ....x.......x...|....x.......x.x.
  hat    x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x.
  tithe  x.....x.....x...|..x.....x.....x.|....x.....x.....|x.....x.....x...

order  intro a b a tithe_break build b turn
